course: dictionary
lesson: 9052
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the sentence around the word. «Sleepwalk» is a verb, a doing word. Its first meaning is to walk or do things while you are asleep, without knowing it.
explain: Look at this: «Sleepwalking and sleep-talking are common in children and usually harmless.» The words common and harmless are clues. They tell you it happens often and is usually not dangerous. Sleepwalking happens during sleep. Nobody plans it while they are awake.
explain: The second meaning is informal, which means it is used in everyday talk rather than formal writing. «Sleepwalking into trouble» means moving into a bad situation without noticing or thinking. Here the word has nothing to do with sleep. Test it: does "moving into trouble without noticing" fit the sentence? Yes, so that is the meaning.
fact: Sleepwalking means walking or doing things while asleep, without knowing it.
fact: «Sleepwalk» is a verb: sleepwalks, sleepwalked, sleepwalking.
fact: A person who sleepwalks is called a sleepwalker.
fact: Sleepwalking is common in children and usually stops as they grow.
fact: If someone sleepwalks, gently guide them back to bed and lock the doors to keep them safe.
exercise: «Sleepwalking and sleep-talking are common in children.» What does sleepwalking mean here? | Walking very fast in a race | Sitting up in bed to read a book | Talking loudly to friends | *Walking or doing things while asleep
exercise: Ella says sleepwalking is always dangerous. What do the words «usually harmless» tell you? | *It is usually not dangerous | It is always dangerous | It only happens to grown-ups | It is a kind of game
exercise: Which meaning fits «sleepwalking in the dark, with eyes shut»? | Moving into trouble without noticing | Talking to a friend at night | *Walking while asleep | Sleeping very late in the morning
test: Which is the past tense of sleepwalk? | *Sleepwalked | Sleepwalker | Sleeping bag | Sleepy
test: What should you do if someone is sleepwalking? | Lead them outside to see the stars | Make them stay up and play a game | Leave the doors open so they can wander | *Gently guide them back to bed
exam: In «sleepwalking into trouble», what does sleepwalking mean? | *Moving into a bad situation without noticing | Dreaming about a trip | Walking in a deep sleep at night | Sleeping very late
